    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Frequency",
     "texto": [
      "**Immer** (always), **oft** (often), **manchmal** (sometimes), **nie** (never). They go after the verb.",
      "**Nie** is already negative: it doesn't take «nicht». **Ich arbeite nie am Sonntag** (I never work on Sundays).",
      "**Doch** is a special «yes»: it is used to contradict a negative sentence."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Go and do",
     "texto": [
      "**Gehen** (to go) and **machen** (to do) are regular: **ich gehe, du gehst, er geht**; **ich mache, du machst, er macht**.",
      "To go somewhere, **in** + accusative is used; with neuter nouns, **in das** contracts to **ins**: **ins Kino**, **ins Schwimmbad**.",
      "**Mit** = with: **mit Freunden** (with friends)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
